<title>USA: NYCE cotton called to open little changed.</title>
<headline>NYCE cotton called to open little changed.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>NYCE cotton futures were called to open mostly unchanged Friday, based on market orders at 1019 EDT, dealers said.</p>
<p>They expect another rangebound and thinly traded session amid a lack of fundamental news.</p>
<p>July cotton settled 0.02 cent weaker at 73.10 cents a lb Thursday after trading from 73.40 to 73.05 cents. New-crop December went out 0.03 cent lower at 75.62 cents.</p>
<p>Volume was estimated at 8,500 lots.</p>
<p>((Suzanne Rostler, New York Commodity Desk, 212-859-1640))</p>
